WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.276
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 3.

2
00:00:04.896 --> 00:00:08.217
How many times does the cout inside the while one loop run?

3
00:00:09.918 --> 00:00:12.587
Count the passes that actually reach line eight.

4
00:00:12.587 --> 00:00:16.032
Pass one prints, pass two prints, and pass three prints.

5
00:00:16.651 --> 00:00:19.651
On pass four, i is three, the break fires on line

6
00:00:19.651 --> 00:00:22.440
five, and the loop ends before line eight.

7
00:00:24.041 --> 00:00:26.315
while of one never stops by itself.

8
00:00:26.315 --> 00:00:29.077
Its exit is the break, so count the passes that

9
00:00:29.077 --> 00:00:32.164
get past the break, not the passes that start.

10
00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:36.434
So the cout inside the loop runs three times.

11
00:00:37.254 --> 00:00:40.751
Counting loop passes instead of passes that reach the cout.

12
00:00:40.751 --> 00:00:43.454
Four passes start, but only three print.

13
00:00:44.174 --> 00:00:48.626
Exam tip: for how many times does it run questions, mark the statement in the

14
00:00:48.626 --> 00:00:52.450
code and tick it in your trace each time the highlight reaches it.
